<!-- Golden case G: the P0 temporal bug, fixed at the solver instead of worked around in Python.

     One invoice, one `<abrechnungsfall>` — one patient. GOÄ 34 on 2026-01-05, GOÄ 4 on 2026-06-20,
     5.5 months later.

     excl_auto_34_4 (data/rules/exclusions.csv, verified=true, direction=one_way): GOÄ 4 is not
     chargeable "neben" (alongside) GOÄ 34. "Alongside" is a clinical term — the two services
     rendered at the same encounter — not an invoice-level one, and before this fix the rules
     engine matched on Ziffer alone with no date dimension at all, so two positions five months
     apart were treated exactly like two positions on the same afternoon.

     `logic/datalog/goae_rules.dl` LAYER 3 now carries `datum(Z, Date)` and derives
     `blocked_exclusion_cross_date` instead of `blocked_exclusion` when the two Ziffern are known
     to have been rendered on different dates. `app/padnext/audit.py` reads that off
     `BlockedCode.cross_date` and routes the position to `unconfirmed` rather than
     `confirmed_wrong`: the invoice alone does not prove the exclusion does NOT apply, only that
     this engine cannot say it does — a human still has to look at it.

     Grouping (case F) does not fix this one: both positions are already in the same, single
     `<abrechnungsfall>`, so this is specifically the date dimension at work, not the patient
     boundary.

     Synthetic data throughout: echtdaten="0". -->
